js/zap.js zap_over_floor() runs on every square a ray crosses and does nothing at all on ordinary room floor, which is the only terrain the goal hero-zaps-a-ray-wand admits. Seven terrains raise UnsupportedZapError instead of acting, each named for the C function it stands in for:

- a web the fire arm burns away (zap.c:5165-5171, delfloortrap());
- ice it melts (5173-5174, melt_ice());
- water it boils (5175-5227, create_gas_cloud(), the POOL that becomes ROOM and the PIT maketrap() leaves in it);
- a fountain it dries (5228-5233, dryup());
- water, lava or ice a cold bolt freezes or firms (5238-5334, start_melt_ice_timeout() and obj_ice_effects());
- iron bars a lightning or acid bolt melts (5344-5369, dissolve_bars());
- a secret door the bolt reveals (5397-5409, cvt_sdoor_to_door()) and a closed door it burns away or is absorbed by (5411-5487, add_damage() and recalc_block_point()).

An eighth stop is one frame lower: OBJ_AT(x, y) with a fire bolt reaches burn_floor_objects(), whose hero-caused half js/zap_destroy_items.js:198-202 already refuses because useupf() charges a shopkeeper for what it burns.

Each of these is a live refusal rather than a divergence: the segment ends at the square, after the beam has been drawn as far as it reached. scripts/zap-ray.test.mjs pins two of them directly -- the cold arm over a POOL square and burnarmor()'s wet towel -- and the rest by the refusal-name list in scripts/zap-command.test.mjs.

A reproducible input for the water arm, which needs no wizard-mode terrain wish: replay scripts/run-ray-zap.mjs's first segment as far as the wish, set the square west of the hero to POOL, and zap a wand of cold west. scripts/zap-ray.test.mjs "a cold bolt over water stops at the steam it would raise" does exactly that and asserts the stop. A C recording of the same shape needs a level whose room adjoins water, which mklev.c does not build at depth 1; the seed scan scripts/run-fire-command.mjs records for its liquid case (7320232) is the nearest one found so far.

What closes it: porting the arms, one terrain at a time, with a fresh differential for each. None of them belongs to the current goal, whose witness crosses plain dark room floor and one wall.
